{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design", "label": "Windows App (GUI + standalone exe) - Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_one_exe_two_entry_modes", "label": "One exe, two entry modes (GUI / --headless)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same frozen exe runs the GUI when launched normally and runs a solve then exits when launched with --headless <cfg.json>. The GUI spawns the solve by re-invoking itself (sys.executable + --headless) so no separate Python interpreter is needed on the target machine; a dev checkout spawns 'python headless_solve.py <cfg>' instead."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_subprocess_solve_isolation", "label": "Subprocess solve with live log, Cancel = kill", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Running the solve in a QProcess crash-isolates it from the GUI; merged stdout streams the IPOPT log live, Cancel kills the process (partial output left in output_dir), and a non-zero exit is reported while the log is kept for inspection."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_thin_gui_layer", "label": "Thin GUI layer / testable plain modules", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All non-Qt logic (config build/serialise, results parse) lives in plain modules that import without a display so they are unit-testable; Qt widgets are thin construction code and are not auto-tested (no display in CI)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_vehparams_two_phase_refactor", "label": "vehParams two-phase refactor (primaries + overrides -> derived)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Safety-critical: vehParams hardcoded primaries and computed derived quantities (ms, m, l_f, l_r, dampers, m_eff, static loads, xti/xsi/lsi, mirrored camber) inline, so applying overrides afterwards would leave every derived value stale - silent wrong physics. Fix: build a primaries dict, merge vp_overrides into it, then derive everything from the merged dict. Contract: byte-for-byte defaults with no overrides (incl. the Rw/gear quirk and Copy-B tyre set), unknown keys raise, mf block overridable but absent from default.json."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_vp_overrides", "label": "vp_overrides dict", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single merged dict of vehParams primary/mf overrides threaded as a vp_overrides kwarg through userOpts and MLTP's **useropts_kwargs; a preset file is itself a vp_overrides dict; the Tier-1 GUI tunables fold into it before serialisation."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_cfg_json", "label": "cfg.json solve configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GUI form -> RunConfig -> cfg.json -> headless_solve.py -> MLTP(**run_kwargs, vp_overrides=...). Three groups: run-config (circuit, AeroConfig, ATD, Electric_4Motors, TyreModel, vi, ni, linear_solver, save, plot, output_dir), Tier-1 tunables, and vp_overrides."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_atd_em4_gui_conflict_rule", "label": "GUI disables ATD while 4-motors is On", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ATD=On with Electric_4Motors=On is forbidden; the underlying code auto-flips ATD -> Off with a warning, so the GUI must instead disable the ATD control while 4-motors is On, leaving no silent change."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_writable_output_dir", "label": "Writable output dir (Documents\\FullModelSim)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A frozen exe may live in read-only Program Files, where writing Results/ and Plots/ relative to the working directory would crash; default output_dir is %USERPROFILE%\\Documents\\FullModelSim, created on first run, editable in the GUI and passed through cfg.json; results panel reads from it."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_pyinstaller_bundling", "label": "PyInstaller bundling (data + native libs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Circuits/*.mat, Data/DATA_AA.mat and app/presets/*.json are collected and resolved at runtime via sys._MEIPASS; CasADi's compiled DLLs plus IPOPT/MUMPS are collected by the hook; build one-folder first (easier DLL debugging), then one-file for shipping."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_frozen_hsl_path", "label": "Frozen-path HSL resolution (sys._MEIPASS)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bundle the Coin-HSL bin DLLs and patch functions/hsl.py to also resolve the DLL directory from the frozen root in addition to COINHSL_DIR / the seeded default; if HSL fails the existing MUMPS fallback keeps the exe solving, so HSL is a performance bonus, not a hard dependency."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_tier1_tunables", "label": "Tier-1 tunables (7 GUI fields)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "brkB, Tdist, ksD, alpha_FL, alpha_FR, alpha_RW, alpha_TW - vehParams primaries exposed as Setup-tab widgets in v1 instead of a 40-field form (YAGNI); folded into vp_overrides. Later superseded by the full vp dict."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_acceptance_floor", "label": "Acceptance floor (clean VM, Sturn on MUMPS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The built exe on a clean Windows VM with no Python must launch the GUI, run Sturn end-to-end with the MUMPS linear solver, stream the IPOPT log live, write results + plots to the Documents output folder and open a plot in the browser; HSL working in the frozen app is a stretch goal."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_expert_config_file", "label": "Expert config JSON file", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full vehParams overrides for power users live in editable JSON text files loaded via a 'Load config' picker on the Advanced tab; shipped default.json is the baseline car."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design_results_summary_panel", "label": "Results summary + plot list (opened in browser)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Summary numbers (lap time, energy) parsed from the saved .mat plus a list of generated Plotly HTML plots each opened in the default browser; no embedded Chromium/QWebEngine."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design", "target": "app_main_main", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design", "target": "app_main_is_headless", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_06_24_windows_app_gui_design", "target": "app_mainwindow_mainwindow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-windows-app-gui-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}